{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Extend the survived-LLM-step-failure tally to review-code and verify-completion\n\n## Context (verified at origin/main cc69cc1179)\n\n`eclectic-industrial-argali` landed a run-scoped sink (`src/rebar/llm/step_failures.py`) that\ncounts LLM step calls which fail but do NOT fail the run, surfaced on the plan-review verdict as\n`coverage.llm_step_failures`. It was scoped to `review-plan` only. The recording site is already\nuniversal: every LLM call funnels through `PydanticAIRunner.run`'s except block\n(`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:595`), which calls `step_failures.record(...)` unconditionally. So both\nremaining gates start counting the moment a scope is active around them — this ticket is scope\nactivation plus a drain.\n\nReference shape, plan-review: activation `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:163`\n(`collect_step_failures()`), drain `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:526-528`\n(present ONLY when non-empty).\n\n## review-code (wiring only)\n\nIt already has a `coverage` object (`src/rebar/schemas/code_review_verdict.schema.json`) and an\nexact structural twin to copy: the contract-violation drain at\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py:521-523`.\n\n1. Activate the sink in the code-review run scope —\n   `gate_dispatch.py:480`, currently\n   `with gate_source.gate_read_root(handle), review_kernel.collect_contract_violations():`.\n2. Drain into that gate's coverage beside the violations drain\n   (`code_review/workflow_ops.py:521-523`), same present-only-when-non-empty posture.\n3. Declare `coverage.llm_step_failures` in `code_review_verdict.schema.json`, mirroring the\n   `plan_review_verdict.schema.json` block verbatim (`required: [total, by_step]`, `total`\n   integer minimum 1, `by_step` object of integers minimum 1).\n\n## verify-completion (needs the placement decision)\n\n`completion_verdict.schema.json` has NO `coverage` object — its properties are `verdict`,\n`findings`, `criteria`, `summary`, `remediation`, `target`, `reviewers`, `certifiable`,\n`runner`, `model`, `trace_id`. The parent ticket explicitly left the placement open (its\nclosing comment: \"verify-completion has no coverage object at all, so it needs a placement\ndecision first\"), and nothing in either ticket's recorded context decides it.\n\n**Decision: `coverage.llm_step_failures`, mirroring the other two gates**, with `coverage`\ncreated ONLY when the tally is non-empty. Rationale, recorded because it is a judgement call:\n\n- One JSON path (`coverage.llm_step_failures`) then works across all three gates, so a caller\n  reads the tally the same way everywhere. A bespoke top-level key on this one gate would make\n  the tally gate-specific for no gain.\n- Creating `coverage` only when non-empty keeps a clean run's verdict byte-identical, so no\n  empty container appears on the overwhelmingly common path. This matters more here than\n  elsewhere: the completion verdict is SIGNED, and byte-identity on clean runs is the\n  attestation-safety posture the parent established.\n\nWiring:\n\n4. Activate the sink in the completion run scope — `gate_dispatch.py:696`\n   (`with gate_config(cfg):`), so it covers the whole `run_workflow` call.\n5. Drain in `completion_reconcile` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py:251` — the registered step\n   function, no leading underscore), the op that assembles the verdict, immediately before its\n   `return findings.validate_structured(result, _OUTPUT_SCHEMA)` at `:319`. The deterministic\n   `completion_passthrough` arm makes no LLM call, so its tally is empty and its verdict is\n   unchanged.\n6. Declare `coverage` (object, with the same `llm_step_failures` sub-block) in\n   `completion_verdict.schema.json`. The schema is `additionalProperties: true`, so this\n   documents the key rather than unblocking it.\n\n## Constraints (same as the parent)\n\nObservability only: never changes a verdict, an exit code, a signature, or a provenance stamp,\nand no swallow site changes behaviour. Present ONLY when non-empty.\n\n## Tests\n\n- review-code: with a sink scope active and a recorded failure, the code-review coach op puts\n  `coverage.llm_step_failures` on the verdict; with no failure the key is ABSENT.\n- verify-completion: same pair through `completion_reconcile` — and on the clean run assert\n  `\"coverage\" not in verdict`, i.e. no empty container is created.\n- The drained shape validates against each gate's schema (`total` + `by_step`).\n- Both gate run scopes actually activate the sink, asserted at the dispatch level rather than\n  only on the op, so a drain that can never receive anything is caught.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `review-code`: a survived LLM step failure appears at `coverage.llm_step_failures` on the\n      code-review verdict.\n- [ ] `review-code`: a clean run's verdict has NO `llm_step_failures` key.\n- [ ] `verify-completion`: a survived LLM step failure appears at `coverage.llm_step_failures`\n      on the completion verdict.\n- [ ] `verify-completion`: a clean run's verdict has NO `coverage` key at all (no empty\n      container).\n- [ ] The code-review run scope (`gate_dispatch.py:480`) activates `collect_step_failures()`.\n- [ ] The completion run scope (`gate_dispatch.py:696`) activates `collect_step_failures()`.\n- [ ] `code_review_verdict.schema.json` declares `coverage.llm_step_failures` with\n      `required: [total, by_step]`.\n- [ ] `completion_verdict.schema.json` declares `coverage.llm_step_failures` with\n      `required: [total, by_step]`.\n- [ ] No verdict string, exit code, or signature changes on any run: the only observable\n      difference is the added key.\n- [ ] Every touched file stays under the 800-LOC module-size cap (`gate_dispatch.py` is 721 and\n      `gate_ops.py` 340 at origin/main, so this must not push either over).\n- [ ] The placement rationale for `verify-completion` is recorded as a comment on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit` passes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786560442623814001,"uuid":"94224432-c498-4008-9fa2-c9dc962ff3c6"}